{"kind":"report","text":"Evidence supplement to G5 assessment389f159594d1dda04bc6e5b75436b788544eda21. After the assessment was filed, root supplied an actual native observation run. I independently read result.json and verified SHA-256 d22cd784450711dbb16b63981b2c38c2c1ad1d2d3bea137d6fc560854d0f96a7 at /Users/hughpyle/Documents/Codex/2026-09-06/the-atseq-project-is-progressing-well/work/noseq-strfry-native/probes/ff272bd4-1556-4a7b-aa75-a4092802b7d4/result.json. Root executed these probes; I did not rerun them or independently validate the complete build chain. The result identifies strfry source 4cd3cf64850caf47dda46c2a2abbbf3525a64d10, binary SHA-256 028f26b98b0b895ed4d32f83642e3fa25173f3498330e9bfc2567a3fc06ffab4, script SHA-256 9f51c0867f829c3aeb8b0d100db40fb0f771cd54b8da7ebd3bc0e86e11aac480 and build-record SHA-256 545bceac10df0157ce00b5a6b6124d03cba2ac4eebcc042b32e643513284b90b.\n\nThe restricted-count profile records unauthenticated kind1 REQ rejected as auth-required, while unauthenticated COUNT{} and COUNT{ids:[the restricted event id]} both return count1. The exact-pin source hypothesis in assessment section2 now has root-executed local corroboration; it is not a reviewer-executed conformance rerun. NEG and other ACL/gateway/freshness paths remain unexecuted in this assessment.\n\nThe size profiles record 65,536-byte events accepted with matching readback and 65,537 rejected under maxEventSize65,536. Raising maxEventSize alone to 131,072 with maxFrameSize131,072 causes a 131,082-byte EVENT message containing a 131,072-byte event to close. With maxFrameSize131,200 the 131,072-byte event is accepted/read back and 131,073 rejected. Specify event and serialized protocol-message/frame budgets separately in G4/G5. These measurements establish no universal plaintext budget and do not replace selected-wrapper, Unicode, encryption/padding, retained-proof and other message-shape measurements.\n\nRoot reports pinned extracted local dependencies allowed this host's native build without global installation, resolving the previously reported local native execution obstacle; the retained result identifies build provenance and stopped-process statuses. This does not resolve bare strfry's membership limitation or adopt the proposed gateway/policy. All recommendations, freshness tradeoffs, fixture requirements and explicit G5/P5 non-pass qualifications in the main report remain in force.","body":{"no_git_artifact":"true","supplements":"git:sha1:77aeeeb3fa42aeb6babdf961f6397ba73fada68b#git:sha1:389f159594d1dda04bc6e5b75436b788544eda21"}}